WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:19.578
When Joy opened the gate to the chicken coop, the six chickens ran to her, squawking.

2
00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:21.930
They were big, fat hens now.

3
00:00:21.931 --> 00:00:25.931
Katie emptied a tin pan of corn onto the ground.

4
00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:31.263
Joy went into the coop and returned with a handful of eggs.

5
00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:36.441
"I worked hard picking up walnuts yesterday," she said to the chickens.

6
00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:38.451
"But you were lazy.

7
00:00:38.452 --> 00:00:43.546
You laid only three eggs! Tomorrow I expect six!"

8
00:00:43.547 --> 00:00:47.418
The chickens ignored her and pecked at the corn.

9
00:00:47.419 --> 00:00:51.790
"Twenty-five dollars and fifty cents isn't bad, Joy.

10
00:00:51.791 --> 00:00:58.289
Didn't Grandpa say that was enough to buy a good set of fiddle strings?" Katie asked.

11
00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.401
One of the chickens pecked at her shoe.

12
00:01:01.402 --> 00:01:04.850
"Yes, but tomorrow the price of walnuts drops."

13
00:01:04.851 --> 00:01:07.834
Joy bent down to pet a chicken.

14
00:01:07.835 --> 00:01:10.953
Then she jumped up, and the hens scattered.

15
00:01:10.954 --> 00:01:14.207
"So today I better get busy!"

16
00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:18.051
The empty garden cart was waiting in the front yard.

17
00:01:18.052 --> 00:01:21.559
Katie and Joy worked all through the morning.

18
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.292
They filled and emptied bucket after bucket.

19
00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:30.785
But when they finished the second tree, the cart was still not full.

20
00:01:30.786 --> 00:01:33.779
"Now what?" said Katie.

21
00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.043
"Now we ask Magoo to help us," said Joy.

22
00:01:38.044 --> 00:01:42.574
They both looked at Magoo, who was asleep under the tree.

23
00:01:42.575 --> 00:01:45.628
Then they heard a voice calling to them.

24
00:01:45.629 --> 00:01:53.402
"Katie! Joy! Hi!" It was Olivia, pedaling down Blackberry Road.

25
00:01:53.403 --> 00:01:56.833
"Hello!" shouted the twins.

26
00:01:56.834 --> 00:02:01.744
Olivia rode up the driveway and dropped her bike in the grass.

27
00:02:01.745 --> 00:02:06.732
"I was hoping you would be outside picking up walnuts," she said.

28
00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:09.605
"There are no black walnut trees in the city.

29
00:02:09.606 --> 00:02:13.631
I've never even tasted a black walnut!"

30
00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:20.939
"Well, when we finish this harvest, we'll ask Grandpa to make some black-walnut ice cream," said Joy.

31
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.901
"You'll love it."

32
00:02:22.902 --> 00:02:27.043
"Black-walnut ice cream?" Olivia said in surprise.

33
00:02:27.044 --> 00:02:29.306
"There's such a thing?"

34
00:02:29.307 --> 00:02:33.728
Before the twins could answer, Olivia looked around on the ground.

35
00:02:33.729 --> 00:02:36.401
"Where are the walnuts?"

36
00:02:36.402 --> 00:02:40.063
"We picked up all the ones by the house," said Katie.

37
00:02:40.064 --> 00:02:43.482
"We were just wondering where to go next."

38
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:47.050
"We can go up by the pond," said Joy.

39
00:02:47.051 --> 00:02:50.687
"We'll have to ask Dad to move the cart."

40
00:02:50.688 --> 00:02:54.991
Just then a walnut fell from a branch onto Joy's head.

41
00:02:54.992 --> 00:02:57.654
"Ouch!" she cried.

42
00:02:57.655 --> 00:02:59.019
"Did you see that?"

43
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.052
The girls looked up into the tree.

44
00:03:02.053 --> 00:03:06.329
"There are still lots of nuts up there," said Olivia.

45
00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.558
"Probably enough to fill the cart," said Joy.

46
00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:14.412
"I wish they would fall down," said Katie.

47
00:03:14.413 --> 00:03:16.075
Then she grinned.

48
00:03:16.076 --> 00:03:18.856
"I've got a great idea!"

49
00:03:18.857 --> 00:03:22.633
She ran to the tree trunk and swung her leg up.

50
00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:26.203
Magoo opened his eyes and looked at Katie.

51
00:03:26.204 --> 00:03:31.283
"See you later, Magoo," said Katie and started to climb the tree.

52
00:03:31.284 --> 00:03:35.021
"There she goes," said Olivia.

53
00:03:35.022 --> 00:03:40.205
"Katie, that is a bad idea," called Joy.

54
00:03:40.206 --> 00:03:43.063
"Just watch!" said Katie.

55
00:03:43.064 --> 00:03:47.583
She pulled herself up and stepped onto a low branch.

56
00:03:47.584 --> 00:03:50.653
"Be careful," said Olivia.

57
00:03:50.654 --> 00:03:54.606
"You're going to fall," said Joy.

58
00:03:54.607 --> 00:03:59.749
Katie pulled herself up higher and stepped onto the next branch.

59
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.314
"Don't go any further," warned Joy.

60
00:04:03.315 --> 00:04:05.791
Katie grabbed a branch above her head.

61
00:04:05.792 --> 00:04:08.848
Then she started bouncing.

62
00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:11.382
"Stop that!" yelled Joy.

63
00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.917
Walnuts rained down from the tree.

64
00:04:13.918 --> 00:04:18.206
Magoo barked. Olivia and Joy screamed.

65
00:04:18.207 --> 00:04:21.813
The two girls ran from the falling nuts.

66
00:04:21.814 --> 00:04:26.245
"Look out below!" yelled Katie.

67
00:04:26.246 --> 00:04:31.900
"Stop that, Katie!" Joy yelled back. "Come down right now!"

68
00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:34.300
Katie bounced more and more.

69
00:04:34.301 --> 00:04:36.170
The nuts kept falling.

70
00:04:36.171 --> 00:04:38.747
Suddenly her foot slipped.

71
00:04:38.748 --> 00:04:41.605
"Katie!" screamed Olivia.

72
00:04:41.606 --> 00:04:46.923
Katie crashed through the branches and landed with a thud.

73
00:04:46.924 --> 00:04:50.413
Joy rushed to her sister and dropped to her knees.

74
00:04:50.414 --> 00:04:52.499
"Are you okay?"

75
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:57.660
"Ow," said Katie. "My ankle hurts."

76
00:04:57.661 --> 00:05:00.212
"Don't move," said Joy.

77
00:05:00.213 --> 00:05:02.936
She ran toward the house.

78
00:05:02.937 --> 00:05:10.111
"MOM! DAD! GRANDPA! Katie fell out of a walnut tree!"
